Engineering Notes

Engineering Observations

SO-F-003 establishes the interpretation stage between environmental perception and adaptive decision generation within the AVIA Functional Objective architecture.

Its primary architectural responsibility is to transform relevant observations into an operationally meaningful context without assuming responsibility for subsequent decision selection or action execution.

---

Engineering Considerations

The interpretation capability should remain sufficiently independent from both perception and decision generation to permit changes within either neighboring capability without unnecessarily propagating changes across the architecture.

Interpretation may operate on incomplete, changing, or uncertain observations. Such conditions should be represented through appropriate engineering mechanisms rather than being implicitly treated as certainty.

---

Known Limitations

This objective establishes the required interpretation capability but does not define:

- Specific interpretation algorithms.
- Artificial intelligence or machine-learning models.
- Context representation technologies.
- Decision-making strategies.
- Action-selection mechanisms.
- Vehicle-control mechanisms.

These shall be established through derived objectives and associated engineering artifacts where required.

---

Future Considerations

Future interpretation objectives may further define capabilities related to:

- Context construction.
- Relationship analysis.
- Situation interpretation.
- Context change detection.
- Interpretation confidence.
- Management of incomplete or ambiguous observations.

Such capabilities shall remain traceable to SO-F-003 if formally derived.

---

Architectural Note

SO-F-003 currently represents an independent interpretation boundary within the AVIA adaptive processing architecture.

The continued validity of this boundary shall be evaluated through subsequent Engineering Review Gates as additional Functional, Safety, Coordination, and other objective domains are developed.

No architectural pattern shall be promoted to a repository-wide standard solely on the basis of this objective.
